==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|LL.|en}} {{m|la|prisma}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|πρίσμα||something sawed}}, from {{m|grc|πρίζειν||to saw}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-prism.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{IPA|/pɹɪzm/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪzm|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪzəm|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|geometry}} A [[polyhedron]] with [[parallel]] ends of the same size and shape, the other faces being [[parallelogram]]-shaped sides.
# A transparent block in the shape of a prism (typically with triangular ends), used to split or reflect light.
# A crystal in which the faces are parallel to the [[vertical]] [[axis]].

